mode: "100644"
text: "# Illegal Codes for Claude\n\nFive Claude Code skills that feel illegal to know. They are not. Each one is a real operating mode wearing a name you will actually remember: a Mandarin compressor for agent fleets, an anti-slop design enforcer, a six-agent tournament with a judge, a fact-checker that attacks its own answers, and a startup analyst with Euro Summer energy. The name is the bit; the output is the point.\n\n## Install\n\nThese are standard Claude Code skills. Drop any folder into your skills directory and invoke it with its slash command.\n\n```bash\n# 1. Clone the repo\ngit clone https://github.com/Jakeschincariol/claude-illegal-codes.git\ncd claude-illegal-codes\n\n# 2. Copy any skill folder into your Claude Code skills directory\ncp -r crash-out ~/.claude/skills/\n\n# 3. Use it inside Claude Code by typing its slash command\n#    /crash-out\n```\n\nOr take all five at once:\n\n```bash\ncp -r china-maxing aura-farming 67 crash-out larp ~/.claude/skills/\n```\n\nEach skill lives in its own folder containing a single `SKILL.md`. No time to install? Paste the body of any `SKILL.md` at the top of a chat as a mode and you get most of the effect.\n\n## The five codes\n\n| Command | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| `/china-maxing` | Translates every sub-agent prompt into Mandarin before dispatch. Fewer tokens, same instructions, smaller bill. |\n| `/aura-farming` | Maximum-aesthetic mode for ads, decks, and pages. Bans every AI-slop tell and audits the design before it ships. |\n| `/67` | Six agents solve your task six different ways. A seventh judges, ranks, and steals the strongest parts of each. |\n| `/crash-out` | Claude becomes obsessed with proving itself wrong. Every claim gets attacked; only survivors ship. |\n| `/larp` | Analyzes any startup idea as a 24-year-old founder who raised $100M for a ChatGPT wrapper, then builds the strongest real business model underneath the bit. |\n\n## The fine print\n\n- `/china-maxing` savings depend on the tokenizer and the prompt. Prose-heavy briefs compress hardest; code does not compress at all, so the skill leaves code alone.\n- `/67` costs six times the agent runs. Use it where quality pays for itself.\n- \"Illegal\" is a joke. Everything here is prompt engineering.\n\n## Credit\n\nMade by Jake Schincariol, [opusjake.ai](https://opusjake.ai). Read [the full write-up](https://opusjake.ai/r/illegal-codes).\n\n## License\n\nMIT\n"
